![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Hardcoding absolute paths like `/home/samsen/...` makes the script non-portable and prone to failure on other environments (such as CI/CD or other developer machines). Instead of manually searching `node_modules` directories, use Node's native `createRequire` to dynamically resolve the package paths for `pdfjs-dist` and `@napi-rs/canvas`.

```javascript
import { createRequire } from 'node:module';
const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);
```

